  "starterCode": "def solve(rows):\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, mathematically sound implementation.\n\n### ⚡ Implementation\n```python\ndef solve(rows):\n    # rows: [{\"department\":..., \"employee\":..., \"salary\":...}]; ties retained\n    maxima={}\n    for r in rows: maxima[r[\"department\"]]=max(maxima.get(r[\"department\"],float(\"-inf\")),r[\"salary\"])\n    return [r for r in rows if r[\"salary\"]==maxima[r[\"department\"]]]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$",
